  "id": "COMPOUND:21516 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 15alpha-Hydroperoxy-guaia-1(10),11-diene may act as a target for prostate cells through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is linked to hepatocytes, which in turn are targets of Licochalcone D and terbutaline, both of which have a role in prostate cell activity. This indicates that the compound may influence prostate cells via metabolic or signaling pathways that are shared among hepatocytes and prostate cells. The mechanism appears to involve the activation of downstream targets in these cell types, possibly through enzyme interactions or signaling cascades. The evidence supports a potential role for 15alpha-Hydroperoxy-guaia-1(10),11-diene in prostate cell function, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
